---
description: Each test asserts one observable outcome
alwaysApply: true
---

# One outcome per test

A test is one scenario. Actor, starting point, action, one expected observable. Independent facts get their own test so a failure names the broken outcome.

`refute record.valid?` plus `assert_includes record.errors[:name]` is one validation. Do not bundle name, email, and company in one test.

```ruby
# bad
test "requires name email and company" do
  customer = organizations(:northwind).customers.new
  refute customer.valid?
  assert_includes customer.errors[:name], "can't be blank"
  assert_includes customer.errors[:email], "can't be blank"
  assert_includes customer.errors[:company], "can't be blank"
end
```

```ruby
# good
test "requires name" do
  customer = organizations(:northwind).customers.new
  refute customer.valid?
  assert_includes customer.errors[:name], "can't be blank"
end
```

HTTP is the same. Seeing Acme Corp and not seeing Acme Inc are two tests. `$199.00` and `$99.00` are two tests.
